 🚀 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Financial Modeling Prep ; Chart: Dan Primack/Axios SpaceX on Friday completed its $60 billion acquisition of Cursor, the largest acquisition ever of a VC-backed startup.

 Cursor had raised over $3.3 billion from firms like Thrive Capital, Neo, Alameda Research (yeah, that one), OpenAI Startup Fund, a16z, Dorm Room Fund, BoxGroup, WndrCo, DST, Coatue, and Accel. SpaceX shares closed Friday above their $135 per share IPO price — defying lockup expiration concerns — but still below the first post-float trades at $150 per share.

 
 
